WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:05.190
Things that are, and things that cannot be,

00:06.570 --> 00:08.020
call out,

00:08.020 --> 00:09.570
and blend together.

00:09.900 --> 00:11.570
They become a Mononoke.

00:12.990 --> 00:13.700
To cut,

00:13.990 --> 00:14.620
to stab,

00:15.570 --> 00:16.660
to gouge,

00:16.660 --> 00:18.580
to carve,

00:19.830 --> 00:22.790
are the duties of the sword.

00:24.040 --> 00:26.170
I must learn the Mononoke’s name,

00:26.170 --> 00:28.040
its shape,

00:28.040 --> 00:29.210
its Form.

00:30.090 --> 00:33.630
I must learn its state of being, its Truth,

00:34.220 --> 00:38.510
and the state of its mind, its Regret.

00:39.270 --> 00:43.310
Then, my blade will cleanse it of its fate.

00:45.520 --> 00:48.020
Ghost Cat

01:12.460 --> 01:16.800
The blue moon illuminated

01:16.840 --> 01:20.760
your wandering shadow.

01:21.390 --> 01:25.270
I could never tell you all I wanted to say.

01:25.270 --> 01:30.190
It was so very frustrating.

01:30.270 --> 01:34.070
I think about your faked smile,

01:34.650 --> 01:38.700
and forget all the hot tears we shed.

01:39.160 --> 01:41.370
What do these empty husks,

01:41.410 --> 01:47.210
those empty eyes of yours, reflect, my dear?

01:47.960 --> 01:52.420
The transient quarter moon

01:52.800 --> 01:54.590
hides in a rift in the clouds,

01:54.550 --> 01:56.970
as darkness seeps up from the ground.

01:57.010 --> 02:01.430
Tell me the truth, please.

02:01.760 --> 02:03.600
Are you so despondent

02:03.680 --> 02:08.060
that you still sit alone, sighing?

02:08.520 --> 02:12.020
The Second Act

02:22.110 --> 02:26.950
A Mononoke who wishes its Truth to be known.

02:26.950 --> 02:28.160
Interesting.

02:29.820 --> 02:31.530
The person who committed suicide,

02:32.330 --> 02:35.240
was it that lady?

02:35.240 --> 02:36.250
Lady?

02:36.790 --> 02:38.510
You mean on that stanchion?

02:38.870 --> 02:40.580
Didn’t you all see her?

02:40.580 --> 02:42.090
Isn’t that why you were so surprised?

02:42.090 --> 02:45.420
So, that’s what you meant when
you said there was someone there.

02:45.420 --> 02:47.420
She was standing there, holding the stanchion!

02:47.420 --> 02:50.340
I was so scared when it started moving!

02:50.340 --> 02:53.150
Sh—She was dressed like a fashion model!

02:55.600 --> 02:57.480
She was there, holding a cat!

02:57.480 --> 02:58.820
Ichikawa Setsuko?

03:04.440 --> 03:08.240
Wh—What do you mean? Ichikawa didn’t have a cat!

03:08.240 --> 03:11.870
Why me? Why? Why?

03:12.120 --> 03:15.790
Can’t you see it, sir?

03:15.790 --> 03:17.760
I need the scales,

03:18.200 --> 03:20.720
because I cannot.

03:21.870 --> 03:23.690
Why can only he…

03:23.690 --> 03:27.050
Because he saw it.

03:27.050 --> 03:31.380
This Setsuko-san’s thoughts brought forth the Ghost Cat.

03:31.380 --> 03:36.150
That, at least, is clear.

03:36.150 --> 03:38.690
That voice…

03:39.060 --> 03:40.240
What voice?

03:40.240 --> 03:43.360
“I won’t forgive you.”

03:43.360 --> 03:44.740
That was real?

03:57.910 --> 04:01.590
Did anyone else hear the woman’s voice?

04:03.170 --> 04:05.460
She’s the one who killed herself.

04:05.460 --> 04:09.310
Why do we have to suffer the consequences?

04:20.750 --> 04:22.160
I see.

04:22.190 --> 04:23.940
I see.

04:22.190 --> 04:23.940
Let me out!

04:33.530 --> 04:36.240
Let me out of here!

04:36.240 --> 04:39.250
Please, let me go!

04:47.340 --> 04:49.220
I have to get out of here!

04:49.730 --> 04:51.180
I…

04:51.180 --> 04:53.930
Mayor’s death, Ghost Cat.

04:55.470 --> 04:58.640
Everyone hid something about Ichikawa Setsuko’s death.

04:58.640 --> 04:59.980
Death, eh?

05:00.940 --> 05:02.440
Wh—What do you want now?

05:03.810 --> 05:06.980
Don’t you mean suicide?

05:06.980 --> 05:07.950
Listen up.

05:07.950 --> 05:11.150
Ichikawa Setsuko threw herself off that bridge to her death.

05:11.150 --> 05:12.540
That’s all there is to it.

05:14.400 --> 05:15.830
Tell me, please,

05:17.110 --> 05:20.460
that I might kill the Ghost Cat.

05:20.790 --> 05:24.750
Oh no! Oh no! I have to get back!

05:24.750 --> 05:26.460
She was hit.

05:26.460 --> 05:29.710
However, I never did believe that she committed suicide.

05:29.710 --> 05:30.760
What are you talking about?

05:31.090 --> 05:33.760
You’re the one who testified she was having trouble at work!

05:33.760 --> 05:37.680
Yes, and she really was having trouble.

05:37.680 --> 05:40.350
She had a good lead, but couldn’t follow it through.

05:40.350 --> 05:42.700
No use writing an article with too little information.

05:42.700 --> 05:43.930
That’s why I had to—

05:43.930 --> 05:46.230
Sure she didn’t just give up on it all?

05:46.230 --> 05:52.330
No, she was determined to rise to the challenge.

05:52.330 --> 05:56.450
She was just a newbie reporter, and
a woman to boot, but she had skill!

05:56.450 --> 05:58.530
Her future was incredibly bright.

06:04.120 --> 06:07.120
Say, is there anyone here who saw it happen?

06:07.120 --> 06:09.750
Of course there isn’t!

06:11.210 --> 06:13.090
A witness, eh?

06:13.090 --> 06:16.260
At any rate, the case was closed!

06:16.260 --> 06:17.640
There shouldn’t be any problem with it.

06:18.180 --> 06:21.650
Even this girl here saw Ichikawa Setsuko looking depressed.

06:21.650 --> 06:23.270
What was it you said, then?

06:23.270 --> 06:24.890
Hm?

06:24.890 --> 06:26.810
Is that so?

06:26.810 --> 06:29.400
Um, well, I…

06:29.400 --> 06:31.310
Come on. Spit it out!

06:31.310 --> 06:35.870
The weaker the dog, the louder its bark, eh?

06:35.870 --> 06:36.540
Huh?

06:37.050 --> 06:38.090
Now talk!

06:38.110 --> 06:41.780
Wh—What I said then, was…

06:41.780 --> 06:44.990
It couldn’t be that it wasn’t a suicide, right?

06:44.990 --> 06:45.500
No!

06:45.500 --> 06:47.540
It had to be!

06:49.220 --> 06:50.220
Well, I…

06:50.220 --> 06:52.680
It was so long ago.

06:52.680 --> 06:56.380
But you remembered her name, did you not?

06:56.380 --> 06:59.060
Ichikawa Setsuko.

07:01.090 --> 07:06.430
W—Well, she was in the newspaper, so of course, I remember.

07:06.430 --> 07:08.150
I’m sorry!

07:08.150 --> 07:10.740
Why are you apologizing?

07:10.740 --> 07:14.700
I—I was just talking to myself, you see.

07:14.980 --> 07:17.360
Maybe she’s dead.

07:17.360 --> 07:19.070
I’m so sorry!

07:19.070 --> 07:20.910
Why are you apologizing?

07:20.910 --> 07:23.460
B—Because I don’t remember too well.

07:24.740 --> 07:27.550
I don’t know anything! I saw nothing!

07:27.550 --> 07:29.000
I didn’t do it!

07:30.300 --> 07:31.580
I just…

07:36.550 --> 07:40.800
Come to think of it, the detective told me something!

07:40.800 --> 07:42.020
Told you what?

07:42.020 --> 07:46.810
That there was someone who saw
Setsuko-san walking near the Kirigahara Bridge,

07:46.810 --> 07:49.350
and that was why they were investigating it as a suicide!

07:49.350 --> 07:50.890
But he just said there were no witnesses.

07:50.890 --> 07:52.690
That’s why I thought it was odd.

07:52.690 --> 07:53.910
You just don’t understand.

07:54.310 --> 07:57.400
Her shoes were neatly arranged on top of the bridge.

07:57.400 --> 07:58.690
Wait a moment!

07:58.690 --> 08:03.160
Couldn’t someone have faked her suicide, though?

08:03.160 --> 08:04.490
Yes, that’s right!

08:04.490 --> 08:07.920
You said there was a witness when you came to question me!

08:07.920 --> 08:10.000
Did you ask them leading questions, Kadowaki-san?

08:10.000 --> 08:11.540
What if I did?

08:11.540 --> 08:17.090
Even if I did try to lead them in one direction or
another, nobody said anything to contradict me.

08:17.090 --> 08:18.100
You got a problem?

08:28.890 --> 08:30.980
Setsuko-san’s death

08:32.980 --> 08:34.730
was a faked

08:35.980 --> 08:37.240
suicide.

08:38.020 --> 08:38.990
That is

08:41.940 --> 08:43.280
the Truth.

08:50.160 --> 08:51.200
What?

08:55.380 --> 08:56.380
What’s going on?

08:56.380 --> 08:57.590
Stop! Stop!

08:58.090 --> 08:59.710
Stop! Help me!

08:59.690 --> 09:00.400
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:00.400 --> 09:01.240
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:01.240 --> 09:01.740
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:01.740 --> 09:02.190
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:02.190 --> 09:02.440
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:02.440 --> 09:02.820
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:02.820 --> 09:03.240
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:03.240 --> 09:03.530
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:03.550 --> 09:03.840
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

09:03.840 --> 09:05.680
S—S—Stop!

09:05.680 --> 09:06.480
S—S—Stop!

09:31.120 --> 09:31.960
Were we

09:32.950 --> 09:34.340
rescued?

09:39.290 --> 09:40.540
Thank you, Mr. Driver!

09:40.540 --> 09:41.420
He doesn’t look so good.

09:41.420 --> 09:42.810
Open this door immediately!

09:44.050 --> 09:46.220
I—I—I didn’t…

09:48.100 --> 09:49.140
What do you mean?

09:51.400 --> 09:52.930
I don’t care!

09:52.930 --> 09:54.230
Just open the door!

09:54.560 --> 09:57.240
Unlike you lot, I’ve got work to do.

09:57.240 --> 09:58.860
Why isn’t it opening?

10:00.610 --> 10:01.520
Help me!

10:03.830 --> 10:07.290
We can finally go back, now.

10:07.650 --> 10:09.460
Wait. This is…

10:09.460 --> 10:10.250
We’re home!

10:11.240 --> 10:12.920
We’ve got it!

10:14.040 --> 10:14.800
What is this?

10:14.800 --> 10:15.450
A trap!

10:15.430 --> 10:15.710
A trap!

10:16.080 --> 10:17.720
I don’t care, as long as we can get off.

10:17.720 --> 10:18.850
You cannot.

10:18.850 --> 10:19.720
Do not leave.

10:46.030 --> 10:47.330
M—Mayor?

10:57.410 --> 11:01.460
All this is the Ghost Cat’s doing.

11:03.000 --> 11:10.010
If you leave, your lives will be forfeited.

11:14.270 --> 11:16.320
Help us, Mr. Medicine Seller!

11:16.320 --> 11:17.440
Please!

11:17.440 --> 11:21.030
You seem content to pass comment,
without actually helping the situation.

11:21.510 --> 11:25.550
People are dead! We have to get out of here, now!

11:25.550 --> 11:32.000
Whether you get out or not is entirely up to you.

11:33.100 --> 11:34.750
I’m not the one who won the raffle.

11:34.980 --> 11:38.320
Why, then? I just got on in his place!

11:38.300 --> 11:40.760
Who did, in fact, win?

11:40.780 --> 11:42.530
Who did, in fact, win?

11:42.530 --> 11:43.510
Well…

11:46.740 --> 11:50.100
I’d like you all to tell me.

11:52.000 --> 11:59.670
If we assemble all your stories, it will likely form the Regret.

11:59.670 --> 12:03.110
Um, uh, I—I saw it.

12:05.370 --> 12:08.080
I kept quiet, thinking it wasn’t my business.

12:08.720 --> 12:11.720
I was in a hurry and didn’t think to stop.

12:11.720 --> 12:17.090
When they said it was a suicide in
the newspaper, I figured that was that.

12:17.090 --> 12:18.920
I forgot all about it soon enough.

12:18.920 --> 12:21.730
Man or woman? Which was it?

12:21.730 --> 12:24.610
I don’t remember.

12:24.610 --> 12:28.180
If it wasn’t a suicide, was it

12:28.180 --> 12:29.180
the culprit?

12:29.180 --> 12:31.270
Masao-kun, you…

12:33.410 --> 12:34.660
It itches! It itches!

12:34.660 --> 12:37.230
My eyes hurt! They hurt, but it itches!

12:38.500 --> 12:42.280
I can’t see!

12:44.970 --> 12:46.720
He told us…

12:46.720 --> 12:48.970
He told us the truth!

12:48.970 --> 12:50.640
Why did it have to take Masao-kun?

12:50.640 --> 12:51.580
How the hell should we know?

12:52.100 --> 12:53.930
It seems like you’re all hiding something!

12:53.910 --> 12:56.250
The medicine seller’s the only sane one among you!

12:56.270 --> 12:57.440
I don’t want to die!

12:57.440 --> 13:01.050
Ichikawa was killed by the mayor’s attaché.

13:01.050 --> 13:03.780
That’s my suspicion.

13:03.780 --> 13:07.010
Oh, the truth at last, eh?

13:07.010 --> 13:09.570
I still don’t have any credible evidence.

13:09.570 --> 13:11.680
That’s why I didn’t want to say anything.

13:11.990 --> 13:15.040
Why was the mayor involved?

13:15.020 --> 13:19.350
A lot of people had a vested
interest in this subway’s construction.

13:19.350 --> 13:22.770
Everyone, from the government
to the construction companies,

13:22.790 --> 13:24.860
were tapping into a veritable river of cash.

13:24.860 --> 13:27.920
Those were the allegations that Ichikawa made.

13:27.920 --> 13:29.030
This is a huge scoop!

13:29.430 --> 13:30.470
We have to let everyone know.

13:31.260 --> 13:32.140
Be patient.

13:32.550 --> 13:35.500
I’ll let you publish it, if you track down one more lead.

13:35.890 --> 13:37.750
I can’t just let it rot!

13:37.750 --> 13:40.960
You know who we’re up against. We must be careful.

13:40.960 --> 13:46.940
And then, the night before she died,
Ichikawa told me she had incontrovertible evidence.

13:46.940 --> 13:52.470
Even so, I said I was too busy, and turned her away.

13:52.870 --> 13:56.240
If only I’d listened then, she might still be alive.

13:58.160 --> 14:01.210
The reason why I came today, abandoning my desk job,

14:01.210 --> 14:05.690
was to trace everything back to
the mayor, and avenge her death.

14:05.960 --> 14:08.880
You were involved.

14:08.860 --> 14:11.660
Then, the mayor must have killed Setsuko-san!

14:11.680 --> 14:14.430
I’m shocked the mayor would do something like that.

14:14.430 --> 14:16.640
It’s a pretty common thing.

14:20.390 --> 14:21.350
What is this?

14:23.610 --> 14:26.170
It itches! It itches! Ah, it hurts!

14:37.040 --> 14:39.830
Three more left.

14:39.830 --> 14:41.960
I need all of you to talk.

14:41.960 --> 14:43.040
I won’t!

14:43.040 --> 14:45.340
If I’m just going to die, there’s no use telling!

14:45.340 --> 14:47.880
Besides, she’s the one who lied in the first place!

14:47.880 --> 14:48.300
I wasn’t!

14:48.300 --> 14:51.360
You always seemed suspicious to me!
You’re too ignorant of what happened!

14:51.360 --> 14:53.010
You didn’t see anything at all, did you?

14:52.990 --> 14:54.660
How did you come across this?

14:54.660 --> 14:56.950
How did you come across this?

14:56.970 --> 14:58.540
How did you come across this?

14:58.540 --> 15:00.870
Kinoshita-san’s the worst of you!

15:00.890 --> 15:02.190
He’s the one who ran her over!

15:02.190 --> 15:04.670
I told you, I didn’t!

15:04.670 --> 15:06.960
I thought it was a cat—

15:08.690 --> 15:11.220
What? You knew it was a living thing?

15:11.220 --> 15:15.310
There’re too many cats to stop! I just thought I hit a cat!

15:15.310 --> 15:16.320
You’re terrible!

15:16.320 --> 15:17.700
You didn’t even think to check?

15:17.700 --> 15:21.870
If we stopped for every cat on the
tracks, we’d never keep our schedules!

15:23.290 --> 15:27.460
Even if it was a cat, does life really mean so little to you?

15:27.440 --> 15:31.950
A cat’s life isn’t worth messing
up so many peoples’ schedules for!

15:27.440 --> 15:29.280
You’re awful!

15:31.970 --> 15:36.120
Besides, what about you? You’re
the one who said it was a suicide!

15:38.720 --> 15:39.760
Chiyo-chan,

15:39.760 --> 15:41.120
do you know this woman?

15:41.640 --> 15:45.150
Oh, well, I think I’ve seen her around.

15:45.130 --> 15:47.090
So, you lied about her being a regular customer!

15:47.730 --> 15:48.920
Well—

15:48.920 --> 15:51.260
It looks like the detective is investigating something.

15:51.260 --> 15:54.070
Oh! Maybe I can get into a newspaper, or even a magazine!

15:54.050 --> 15:56.930
You wanted to use the situation for your own personal gain!

15:56.930 --> 15:59.760
Well, I want to be an actress!

15:59.780 --> 16:01.740
I have to be in the papers and stuff to get famous.

16:01.740 --> 16:04.650
Do you really have a face for the stage?

16:41.580 --> 16:43.910
Sakai Shoujiro.

16:44.980 --> 16:48.610
However did you get a hold

16:49.670 --> 16:50.940
of this?

16:53.320 --> 16:55.740
I came in his place.

16:57.490 --> 16:59.120
In his place?

17:00.050 --> 17:03.160
He couldn’t come, you see.

17:06.180 --> 17:07.460
Harlot!

17:07.460 --> 17:11.060
I can see your wrinkles, you old harlot!

17:11.060 --> 17:14.380
Even your dead husband wouldn’t want you now.

17:14.380 --> 17:16.220
I’m no harlot!

17:19.970 --> 17:22.470
Yeah, that’s what I want to know!

17:22.470 --> 17:24.560
Then, what the hell were you doing?

17:24.560 --> 17:27.910
You were out all night! Where were you?

17:27.910 --> 17:30.540
Shut up! I don’t need to listen to you!

17:30.540 --> 17:31.440
You bastard!

17:37.860 --> 17:38.970
I can’t believe you!

17:39.380 --> 17:41.970
Something like that could have been extremely useful!

17:41.970 --> 17:45.720
If only you’d told the truth, it
wouldn’t have been called a suicide!

17:45.720 --> 17:48.230
Poor Setsuko-san!

17:48.230 --> 17:50.060
Tell the truth?

17:50.060 --> 17:53.770
That’s rich, coming from your mouth.

17:53.770 --> 17:55.800
I was close enough to the truth.

17:56.110 --> 17:58.510
You should be arrested for perjury!

17:58.510 --> 18:00.700
I just didn’t say anything!

18:00.700 --> 18:03.410
Your crime was the worst of all. I’m sure of it!

18:03.810 --> 18:05.950
The mayor’s the only criminal!

18:05.950 --> 18:07.690
Right, Mr. Medicine Seller?

18:11.170 --> 18:13.980
You were listening well.

18:15.690 --> 18:19.260
My mother-in-law didn’t even know I was out!

18:19.260 --> 18:21.590
I couldn’t say anything!

18:25.640 --> 18:28.350
You chose your own happiness over truthful testimony?

18:28.350 --> 18:29.810
That’s just wrong!

18:29.810 --> 18:31.690
I don’t want to hear it from you!

18:31.690 --> 18:33.420
Put yourself in my shoes!

18:33.770 --> 18:37.320
I had to leave while my
mother-in-law was asleep and be back by dawn!

18:37.320 --> 18:39.510
I had to be very careful!

18:39.510 --> 18:43.780
Are you saying I should have just stayed
celibate after my damned husband died?

18:43.780 --> 18:46.100
Maybe you should have!

18:46.100 --> 18:50.080
Yeah, right. I saw you eyeing the
medicine seller not minutes ago!

18:50.080 --> 18:51.410
What are you talking about?

18:52.460 --> 18:54.960
Cat fights are so ugly.

18:54.960 --> 18:56.460
Oh man, oh man.

18:56.460 --> 18:58.940
Oh man, oh man, oh man.

18:57.920 --> 18:58.960
This is all thanks to you not stopping your damn train!

18:58.950 --> 19:02.320
This is all thanks to you not stopping your damn train!

19:02.320 --> 19:05.800
I was just doing my job!

19:05.800 --> 19:07.930
I didn’t stop because I thought it was a cat!

19:07.930 --> 19:10.870
But you did hit Setsuko-san, didn’t you?

19:10.870 --> 19:11.790
Shut up!

20:05.600 --> 20:06.740
Oh my.

20:07.850 --> 20:10.270
There’s still more?

20:10.280 --> 20:12.190
There’s still more?

20:48.410 --> 20:50.390
Why don’t we

20:55.690 --> 20:57.160
put an end

20:58.290 --> 21:00.920
to this?

21:05.950 --> 21:10.030
To be continued

21:11.750 --> 21:19.250
Without you, I just can’t smile.

21:20.380 --> 21:30.310
I walk this banal town,

21:30.310 --> 21:36.390
feeling such intense emotions.

21:36.940 --> 21:42.780
I know that if I could treasure them and live on,

21:42.860 --> 21:52.080
I would need nothing else.

21:52.740 --> 22:00.250
The summer flowers that bloomed in the sky

22:00.250 --> 22:06.550
Come falling down, dancing in the wind.

22:06.630 --> 22:09.890
I can barely recall the night sky

22:09.890 --> 22:13.180
where they all came tumbling down,

22:13.180 --> 22:24.030
